BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 11 Tf 54 732 Td (A short story by Mira Sol) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td () Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 700 Td (On Maple Street, between a bakery and a shop that sold old maps, there was a patch) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 684 Td (of ground no wider than a bedsheet. For years it held a tired bench, two stubborn) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 668 Td (weeds, and a sign that said PLEASE KEEP OFF THE GRASS. There was no grass.) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 652 Td () Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 636 Td (Mira passed it every morning on her way to the bus. One rainy Tuesday she noticed) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 620 Td (a paper cup full of soil beside the bench. A green tip leaned out of it. The next) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 604 Td (day she brought a spoon. The day after that, she brought a packet of marigold) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 588 Td (seeds.) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 572 Td () Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 556 Td (She asked the neighbors before she planted anything. Mr. Lee from the bakery) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 540 Td (offered a bucket. Jo, who lived upstairs, brought gloves with one blue thumb. A) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 524 Td (child named Remy painted a wooden sign: PLEASE HELP THE GRASS GROW.) Tj ET
BT 0.18 0.18 0.16 rg /F1 10 Tf 54 508 Td () Tj ET
BT 0.55 0.55 0.50 rg /F1 9 Tf 540 30 Td (1 / 3) Tj ET
